 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The worker uses a 2Q eviction policy. First-use entries enter an in queue; a second access promotes the entry to an out queue that protects reused sheets. Eviction preferentially removes from the in queue, then from the out queue when the 12 GiB bound requires it. The in/out size split is a tunable parameter and will be sized to protect comparison working sets during sequential screenings. All replacement bookkeeping remains private to the preview worker.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q with in/out queues | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | 2Q protects reused comparison sheets from eviction by one-off sequential screening scans, matching the observed editor pattern of long screens followed by repeated comparisons. Extra bookkeeping for two queues and size split is acceptable. LRU offers lower bookkeeping but evicts useful comparison sheets during scans. Frequency with aging retains popular clips longer than needed after project switches and adds counter maintenance. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Eviction policy selected as 2Q to protect reused sheets during screening scans.
+
+### Deferred
+1. In/out queue size split tuning value. To be determined from pilot measurements.
+2. Promotion threshold details for entries moving from in to out.
